  "description": "QEPTIR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 2/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C92 H116 Gd4 O32,C92 H116 Gd4 O32. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.778-3.904 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.32-108.43°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C92H116Gd4O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
